@jerrychen0awi Yes I still have $AAOI and personally think the $6.6b valuation doesn’t price in next year’s inflection happening Q2 next year onward.

I personally modeling somewhere around ~$1.9B quarterly revenue Q4 2027,  ~40% gross margins.

With another bump in blended gross margins as ELSFP comes online Q1 2028.

@PhotonCap I think the more exciting application is robotics/humanoids, which was mentioned in the PR.

With likely $AEVA doing FMCW LiDAR and robotics sensing with LG Innotek and others (Boston Dynamics supplier).

But hard to get visibility over what end product Sivers lasers go into. Regardless, I agree this is a huge step for $SIVE

@cbart2007 Forget the 2030 numbers. Let’s just focus on 2027 for now.

At $8 million per Rubin rack, filling 1 GW entirely with Rubin racks would cost $40 billion. And I think 1 GW of Rubin capacity could generate at least $20 billion, potentially $30 billion or more, in annual revenue. On that basis, the economics aren’t unreasonable.

This really is a profitable business.

